---
// PDF-96 D6/F. NEW. "What a write actually does" -- the atomic-write
// sequence, re-derived 2026-09-20 from src/pdf_tooling/safety/atomic.py's
// own seven-step docstring, compressed to six stations (step 7, crash
// residue, belongs in the evidence below, not the drawing -- it is
// reported by `doctor --strict`, never swept, PLAN.md §12 R-07).
//
// Two tracks, exactly one crossing: everything happens on the scratch
// track; the upper track -- your file -- is untouched until the last
// station, where the two touch once and the crossing is instantaneous.
// That is what "atomic" means, drawn. Placed immediately after the spine:
// it is the L3 detail, and the reader has just been told safety/atomic.py
// is one file.
//
// Station 3 names no temp-file prefix (E7/AC15/AC16): the real prefix, a
// TEMP_PREFIX literal declared once at safety/tempnames.py:30, is a
// registered spelling under src/ and a FORBIDDEN needle under website/ --
// tests/test_website_contract.py's legacy-needle arm and tests/test_
// rename_completeness.py's remainder and residue-count checks both catch
// it if it is ever typed here, and the failure they report reads as a
// brand census, not a diagram defect. This comment deliberately never
// spells the prefix out (it self-matched here once, during drafting, and
// reddened the exact arm this note describes) -- describe it by pointer
// only, in this file and in the rendered station text alike.
import contracts from '../data/contracts.json';
import Prose from './Prose.astro';
import { langOf, pick } from '../lib/i18n';
import { STATIONS_ES, ATOMIC_ES } from '../lib/copy-es';

const { atomicWrite: enAtomic } = contracts;

// The GLYPHS are numerals and the source path is an identifier; both come
// from `contracts.json` in either language. Only the station names, their
// details and the failure line fork.
const atomicWrite = langOf(Astro.url) === 'es'
  ? {
      ...enAtomic,
      stations: enAtomic.stations.map((st, i) => ({ ...st, ...(STATIONS_ES[i] ?? {}) })),
      failure: ATOMIC_ES.failure,
      crossingLabel: ATOMIC_ES.crossingLabel,
    }
  : enAtomic;
const crossingIndex = atomicWrite.stations.length - 1; // the only station on "your file"'s own track

const t = pick(Astro.url, {
  eyebrow: 'Your files',
  heading: 'A run that dies halfway leaves your file untouched',
  introA:
    'Kill the process, lose the disk, pull the power: elsewhere the usual result is a half-written file where your document used to be. Here every step happens on a scratch file next to yours, and your own file is touched once, at the very end, by a rename the operating system cannot leave half-finished. Nothing else in the run can reach it. Only one file in the whole codebase is allowed to write anything (',
  introB:
    '), which is why this holds for every command, not just the ones someone remembered to make safe.',
  legend:
    'Everything before the crossing runs on a scratch file, on the same filesystem as the target; only the last station touches your file, and it does so atomically.',
}, {
  eyebrow: 'Tus archivos',
  heading: 'Si una corrida muere a la mitad, tu archivo queda intacto',
  introA:
    'Mata el proceso, pierde el disco, desconecta la corriente: en otras herramientas el resultado habitual es un archivo truncado donde antes estaba tu documento. Aqu\u00ed cada paso ocurre en un archivo de trabajo junto al destino, y tu propio archivo se toca exactamente una vez, al final, con un rename que el sistema operativo no puede dejar a medias. Nada m\u00e1s en toda la corrida puede alcanzarlo. Para eso sirve la \u00fanica ruta de escritura de abajo: un solo archivo de este c\u00f3digo tiene permiso de escribir (',
  introB:
    '), y por eso la garant\u00eda aplica a todos los comandos y no nada m\u00e1s a los que alguien se acord\u00f3 de hacer seguros.',
  legend:
    'Todo lo que pasa antes del cruce sucede en un archivo de trabajo, en el mismo sistema de archivos que el destino; solo la \u00faltima estaci\u00f3n toca tu archivo, y lo hace de forma at\u00f3mica.',
});
---

<section id="atomic-write" aria-labelledby="atomic-h" class="u-crop mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24">
  <p class="micro text-surface-400">{t.eyebrow}</p>
  <div class="u-reveal-rule mt-3 h-px w-full bg-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <h2 id="atomic-h" class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-surface-50 sm:text-4xl">
    {t.heading}
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg text-surface-300">
    {t.introA}<code class="code-inline code-path text-sm">{atomicWrite.sourcePath}</code>{t.introB}
  </p>

  <ol class="atomic-write mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-6 md:gap-3" aria-describedby="atomic-legend">
    {atomicWrite.stations.map((station: { glyph: string; name: string; detail: string }, i: number) => (
      <li class={`station rounded-md border p-4 ${i === crossingIndex ? 'crossing border-primary-400/60 bg-primary-500/10' : 'border-line-soft bg-surface-950'}`}>
        {i === crossingIndex && (
          <p class="crossing-label micro mb-2 text-primary-400">{atomicWrite.crossingLabel}</p>
        )}
        <span class="glyph block font-mono text-lg text-primary-400" aria-hidden="true">{station.glyph}</span>
        <h3 class="name mt-1 text-sm font-semibold text-surface-50"><Prose text={station.name} /></h3>
        <p class="detail mt-1 text-xs leading-snug text-surface-300"><Prose text={station.detail} /></p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <p class="failure mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-surface-300">
    <span class="text-primary-400" aria-hidden="true">&cross;</span> <Prose text={atomicWrite.failure} />
  </p>

  <p id="atomic-legend" class="legend mt-4 max-w-2xl text-xs text-surface-400">
    {t.legend}
  </p>
</section>
